  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 135 AM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nHighs near or above 100 degrees are expected again for much of west \nTexas and southeast New Mexico on Tuesday. By the middle of the \nweek, upper-level shortwaves push the ridge farther west and help \nlower heights across our area. As a result, highs tick down a couple \nof degrees relative to Monday and Tuesday. Most locations top out in \nthe mid-to-upper 90s through the end of the week, with only the \ntypical warm spots (particularly the Rio Grande and Pecos River \nvalleys) reaching or exceeding 100 degrees. Nevertheless, this means \ntemperatures across the area will remain consistently a couple of \ndegrees above normal through the end of the forecast period. Besides \nisolated shower and thunderstorm chances in the higher terrain (10-\n20%, mainly in the Davis Mountains), most locations stay dry through \nthe extended.\n\nSprang",
